WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.009 --> 00:00:05.328
Wins and losses
—they say that’s the measure of an athlete.

00:00:05.328 --> 00:00:07.602
[Announcer] First championship in franchise history.

00:00:07.602 --> 00:00:10.711
But we can’t separate the athlete from the human.

00:00:10.711 --> 00:00:11.680
[Announcer] He’s receiving heavy boos here.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:12.165
We never could.

00:00:12.165 --> 00:00:14.830
[Mahmoud Abdul-Rauf] ...I look at the African American being oppressed in this country...

00:00:14.839 --> 00:00:15.153
...and I don’t stand for that.

00:00:15.199 --> 00:00:17.609
[Offscreen] The most important factor is respect, period.

00:00:18.959 --> 00:00:22.600
Black athletes are celebrated on the court but feared off of it.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.870
[Journalist] An NBA player tased by police.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:31.080
Their talent is worth millions, but their voices deemed worthless.

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:35.549
But athletes have always and will always fight for victory.

00:00:36.089 --> 00:00:38.450
[LeBron James] We will definitely not “shut up and dribble.”

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:39.890
Not just in basketball…

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:41.060
[Layshia Clarendon] We will be a voice for the voiceless.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:42.070
...but for the culture.

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:45.509
[Journalist] Maya Moore, stepping away from basketball to fight for justice.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:49.390
So we owe it to the game and to the people to share the whole story,

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:51.540
from court to concrete.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.309
[Jaylen Brown] Being an NBA player don’t exclude me from no conversation.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.000
[Protesters] What do we want?

00:00:55.001 --> 00:00:55.500
Justice.

00:00:55.501 --> 00:00:57.830
Because this is bigger than basketball.

00:00:57.831 --> 00:00:59.602
[Protesters] Black lives matter!

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.400
[Dwyane Wade, at 2016 ESPYs:] It has to stop.

00:01:01.401 --> 00:01:02.160
[Natasha Cloud] I want real change in America.

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:03.500
[Paul George] Breonna Taylor, rest in peace.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.939
[Shaquille O'Neal] Can’t separate peace from freedom.

00:01:06.939 --> 00:01:08.270
[Offscreen] Freedom and justice for all.

00:01:08.443 --> 00:01:09.319
[Rev. Jesse Jackson in 1963:] I am

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:10.195
[Crowd, in response] I am

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:10.987
[Jackson] Somebody.

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:11.696
[Crowd] Somebody.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:12.447
[Jackson] I am

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:13.573
[Crowd] I am

00:01:13.656 --> 00:01:14.449
[Jackson] Somebody.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:15.450
[Crowd] Somebody.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:16.367
[Jackson] I am

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:17.202
[Crowd] I am

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.161
[Jackson] Somebody.

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:19.370
[Crowd] Somebody.

00:01:19.537 --> 00:01:20.246
[Jackson] I am

00:01:20.288 --> 00:01:20.997
[Crowd] I am

00:01:21.289 --> 00:01:22.457
[Jackson] Somebody.

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:27.212
[Crowd] Somebody.

